A说成弱酸，A错误。\nB．加水稀释时第二步电离平衡向右移动，但稀释作用占主导，c(H⁺)减小，B正确。\nC．第一步完全电离，第二步HA⁻⇌H⁺＋A²⁻。设第二步电离x mol·L⁻¹，则(0.1＋x)x/(0.1－x)＝1.0×10⁻²，解得x≈0.0084，所以c(H⁺)≈0.1084 mol·L⁻¹，不是0.12 mol·L⁻¹，C错误。\nD．NaHA溶液中第二步电离产生的H⁺为0.02 mol·L⁻¹；在H₂A溶液中，第一步产生的H⁺会抑制第二步电离，故总c(H⁺)＜0.12 mol·L⁻¹，D错误。\n故选B。","expected_stem":"某二元酸(H2A)在水中的电离方程式为H2A===H\n＋＋HA\n－，HA\n－\nH\n＋＋A2－\n(25 ℃时，Ka＝1.0×10\n－2)，下列有关说法中正确的是(\n)\nA.H2A 是弱酸\nB.稀释0.1 mol·L\n－1 H2A 溶液，电离平衡向右移动，c(H\n＋)减小\n－1\nC.在0.1 mol·L\n－1 的H2A 溶液中，c(H\n＋)＝0.12 mol·L\nD.若0.1 mol·L\n－1 NaHA 溶液中c(H\n＋)＝0.02 mol·L\n－1，则0.1 mol·L\n－1 的H2A 中c(H\n－1\n＋)=0.12 mol·L","expected_options":["H2A 是弱酸","稀释0.1 mol·L －1 H2A 溶液，电离平衡向右移动，c(H ＋)减小 －1","在0.1 mol·L －1 的H2A 溶液中，c(H ＋)＝0.12 mol·L","若0.1 mol·L －1 NaHA 溶液中c(H ＋)＝0.02 mol·L －1，则0.1 mol·L －1 的H2A 中c(H －1 ＋)=0.12 mol·L"],"expected_content_fingerprint":"6a03ca02e180325e7566b24f2a73f09b11b9492b0f23f4e53bafbd9055a022d4","audit_status":"FAIL","segment_mode":"ABCD","required_markers":["A","B","C","D"],"new_asset_refs":[{"kind":"question_image","path":"h2orig/661c88a72c37c1d5/7941dc3f001af8b1c9777cffc83aa94c/question/r245be48b2999","alt":"苏教版高中化学原题13原题题面","sha256":"947e79fac82a505ca3806ad8a70b1dc7c16aacdb430c5e7c0853c8cbdf6b67b0","width":1055,"height":334},{"kind":"analysis_image","path":"h2orig/661c88a72c37c1d5/7941dc3f001af8b1c9777cffc83aa94c/analysis/r245be48b2999","alt":"苏教版高中化学原题13原题解析","sha256":"168238741a21f9f8be7740040a84260b70eea5e4aabdace66b1abd666f52ff3f","width":1055,"height":527}],"question_asset_sha256":"947e79fac82a505ca3806ad8a70b1dc7c16aacdb430c5e7c0853c8cbdf6b67b0","analysis_asset_sha256":"168238741a21f9f8be7740040a84260b70eea5e4aabdace66b1abd666f52ff3f","expected_revision_token":"e8774a7556740222637c92e5bbfb1d3a608e686f26a414bdaa5aef8521798851","expected_item_sha256":"8d8ecd1d64fcaa12b1217a87e5163024584ae678c1e3c421edfc667728ec973a","source_pdf_sha256":"1f43e3800520493d33ea368192d9402e19135115e6ba17639826216f81595943","question_png_sha256":"8e39d462c3fb31884ba09eea475913c5541d6789b092ef460453eeac99231442","analysis_png_sha256":"b7f894910c76add8f2c814c9a2aa375d190dd2d7f9742b5c7b7a5244e8ab3700"},{"source_manifest_id":"H2_WEAK-ca1394bd60a7c25b","canonical_source_id":"--:H2_WEAK-ca1394bd60a7c25b","grade_band":"高二","skill_id":"H2_WEAK","old_question_id":"QH2O_40D983E9910CC1FB_305A8870C52C700A_R761DC1B48D41","new_question_id":"QH2O_40D983E9910CC1FB_3A0B914814414758_R245BE48B2999","correct_option":2,"baseline_explanation_sha256":"03e64ecd6ab73776122954c442fde2908cf44c168f73b8fe66d2c5642d7d83a5","expected_explanation_sha256":"03e64ecd6ab73776122954c442fde2908cf44c168f73b8fe66d2c5642d7d83a5","expected_explanation":"A．强酸进入体液后c(H⁺)增大，平衡向左移动并消耗一部分H⁺，有助于维持pH相对稳定，A合理。\nB．强碱进入体液后会消耗H⁺，平衡向右移动并补充一部分H⁺，有助于维持pH相对稳定，B合理。\nC．大量生理盐水使体液被稀释。平衡虽向右移动，但只能减弱稀释造成的变化，最终c(H⁺)减小、pH增大，不是pH减小，C不合理。\nD．CO₂进入血液后推动平衡向右移动，c(H⁺)增大，体液pH减小，D合理。\n故选C。","expected_stem":"已知人体体液中存在如下平衡：CO2＋H2O\nH2CO3\nH\n＋＋HCO\n体液pH 的相对稳定。下列说法不合理的是(\n)\nA.当强酸性物质进入体液后，上述平衡向左移动，以维持体液pH 的相对稳定\nB.当强碱性物质进入体液后，上述平衡向右移动，以维持体液pH 的相对稳定\nC.若静脉滴注大量生理盐水，则体液的pH 减小\nD.进行呼吸活动时，如果CO2 进入血液，会使体液的pH 减小","expected_options":["当强酸性物质进入体液后，上述平衡向左移动，以维持体液pH 的相对稳定","当强碱性物质进入体液后，上述平衡向右移动，以维持体液pH 的相对稳定","若静脉滴注大量生理盐水，则体液的pH 减小","进行呼吸活动时，如果CO2 进入血液，会使体液的pH 减小"],"expected_content_fingerprint":"e22febe7a44b77b14488c4e55c3544433e5190b1a94d8d2d0c6af5f5935c0799","audit_status":"PASS","segment_mode":"ABCD","required_markers":["A","B","C","D"],"new_asset_refs":[{"kind":"question_image","path":"h2orig/40d983e9910cc1fb/6bd28dea016d7e6ceb99fe7dae5705e0/question/r245be48b2999","alt":"苏教版高中化学原题2原题题面","sha256":"8493b43b9cfdfa5b5323ef09fe252ca5d8edaa4364743b4b54e425e9b378911c","width":1055,"height":287},{"kind":"analysis_image","path":"h2orig/40d983e9910cc1fb/6bd28dea016d7e6ceb99fe7dae5705e0/analysis/r245be48b2999","alt":"苏教版高中化学原题2原题解析","sha256":"bc254b1098903f06f0cae958ec63ea10422a004ef805a4619ba2a0ba1b947d8a","width":1055,"height":752}],"question_asset_sha256":"8493b43b9cfdfa5b5323ef09fe252ca5d8edaa4364743b4b54e425e9b378911c","analysis_asset_sha256":"bc254b1098903f0